WEBVTT

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:02.480
What?!

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:06.990
Is that true, Risa? Did they 
really release Level 4?

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.140
<i>It's true. I just found out 
myself, and I can't believe it!</i>

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.610
<i>I thought it wouldn't 
happen until next week.</i>

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.570
A lot of players have 
already gotten to Level 4.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.900
So I guess you hadn't noticed either, huh?

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.090
<i>Oh, man, I can't wait!</i>

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.910
<i>I'm gonna log in right now!</i>

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.420
<i>I'll be right there, too. Let's get the 
gang together and beat the Level 3 boss!</i>

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.330
Yeah!

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:53.900
<b>BOFURI: </b>I <b>Don't Want </b>to <b>Get Hurt,
</b>so I'll <b>Max Out My Defense</b>.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.710
So if we beat this guy, 
we can go to Level 4?

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:21.950
<b>Maxing Defense </b>and <b>Christmas</b>.

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:20.510
Looks tougher than I was expecting.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:22.540
You can leave this one to me!

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.070
[Phantom World]!

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.170
Here we go!

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:50.020
I don't... think we're gonna 
get a taste of this action.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:53.780
I mean, I figured this is 
how it was gonna go, but...

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.360
You're amazing, Maple!

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.180
What a pretty place!

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:20.410
What should we do now? 
Stop by the guild house first?

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.340
Maybe we should scout out the place?

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:25.300
I can't wait to see what Level 4's like!

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.810
Same here!

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.430
Sounds good to me.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.020
I guess gathering information 
is our first priority.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.740
Let's split up and look around, then.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:36.250
We'll meet back up later 
and share what we learned.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.730
Got it!

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:41.070
All right! Let's do this, everyone!

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.830
Yeah!

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:30.790
Well, it's probably about time 
for some monsters to show up...

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.490
Whoa!

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:34.700
Frederica?

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:37.670
You know surprise attacks don't 
actually work, don't you?

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:43.800
I knew you'd be able to 
dodge it if anyone could.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.880
That was just my way of saying hello.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:48.770
You're challenging me to another duel?

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:52.080
Didn't you guys just now 
get to Level 4, too?

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.600
Aw, don't be so cold.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:57.980
I thought up all kinds 
of strategies for this.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.460
Isn't that what you say every time?

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:04.950
Well, I <i>have</i> to when you crush all 
my new strategies right off the bat.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.780
Just one hit!

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:13.080
If I could land just one hit, I could 
give you your first taste of humiliation!

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:18.290
Well, I haven't died once yet, 
and neither has Maple.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.990
Okay, then... wanna get to it?

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:22.620
Let's go!

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:29.930
Oh, so it's always nighttime in Level 4?

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.640
That's so strange.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.100
Huh?

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.510
It's Mii.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.000
Okay.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:44.490
Once I've soothed my soul, 
I'll rejoin the others.

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:46.110
Huh?

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.450
Was that something I wasn't supposed to see?

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.780
Wh-Wh-What should I do?

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:54.660
Right! I should be honest 
and tell her I saw that!

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.870
Fluffy Friends Room

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:59.250
And that I won't tell anyone, 
so she doesn't need to worry!

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.210
Huh?

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:07.010
They're soothing my soul...

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:11.290
Yes, I know. I'll give each of 
you some. Just wait your turn.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:17.550
That little tongue tickles!

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:19.560
Huh?!

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:26.870
Oop!

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.100
They really do soothe the soul!

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.850
They're so cute! So cute!

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:36.410
I know, right? Aren't they adorable?

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:41.750
You really surprised me, though. 
You always look so cool and tough.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:44.710
Well, yeah, when I'm acting as guildmaster.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:47.490
But I don't really care 
if you know about this.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.090
It's not easy keeping up 
the act all the time.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.430
Oh, and you can call me "Mii."

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:54.260
Can I ask you something, then?

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:57.070
Why do you always keep up that act?

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:58.640
Well...

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:01.880
When I first started role playing 
with this character,

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:04.370
everyone seemed to rely on me a lot,

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:06.860
and eventually it got to the point 
where there was just no going back.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.620
I've told Misery about this, kind of,

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:12.390
but I've been keeping it a secret 
from the others in my guild.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:13.860
So that's why...

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:16.130
Yeah, that's why.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:20.540
Got it! I won't tell anyone!

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:24.380
It'll be our little secret, Mii!

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.470
Yeah! Thanks!

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.990
Would you like to go hunting 
together sometime?

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:32.930
Yeah, I'd love to!

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:34.780
Mii!

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.060
Mii, we've been looking for you.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.710
You weren't answering our messages.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:43.060
Oh, Maple is with you?

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:48.040
Y-Yes. We were sharing information 
as fellow guildmasters.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:48.810
Huh?

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:51.400
Oh, yeah! Something like that!

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.670
The other guild members are waiting for you.

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:56.370
They want to hear your strategy 
for beating Level 4.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.500
Mii, please give us your guidance.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.660
All right.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:03.420
See you again soon, Maple.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.380
If you'll excuse us, Maple.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:09.840
O-Of course, Misery and Markus!

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:13.560
<i>I guess Mii's got it rough, too...</i>

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.760
[Multi-Barrier]!

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:19.980
Trying to hold me in place 
right from the get-go?

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.390
That's not gonna work!

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.110
[Multi-Stonebolt]!

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:30.150
You're mine now!

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:42.310
I won!

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:46.040
Sorry. That celebration's 
gonna be short-lived.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:46.920
Huh?!

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:54.570
I lost again!

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:59.050
Ugh, how?! I <i>know</i> I hit you dead-on!

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:02.680
I'm not gonna show my 
precious cards to a rival.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:06.900
I'll beat you next time! Remember that!

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.930
Man, I was so sure I won...

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:11.340
That was too close.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:13.740
I can't afford to let my 
guard down around her.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:18.510
I'm used to fighting her now, but she's 
still a top fighter in a top guild.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.560
Also raises AGI by 50% for one minute.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:23.660
Empty Shell

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:23.660
Once per day, an attack that reduces health from full to zero can be nullified.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:23.660
Conditions for Acquisition

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:23.660
No damage taken from attacks until reaching level 35.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:23.660
A skill that nullifies full-to-zero 
damage just once a day...

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:28.110
It saved my skin back there, but still, 
I gotta get better at dodging.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.210
<i>If I ever do get defeated,</i>

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:35.860
<i>there's only one person who can do it.</i>

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.260
This level's a lot bigger 
than I would've expected.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.260
<b>—One Week Later—</b>

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:44.310
I haven't even reached the tower 
in the center of the town yet.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:47.500
There are still some materials I 
haven't gotten a hold of, too.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.980
This one might take some time to conquer.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:54.090
Yui and I have been riding 
around on rickshaws.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:58.420
It costs some money, but it's 
quicker and easier than walking.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.570
We both move so slowly, after all.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:04.210
I heard the town will be looking different 
soon, since it's almost Christmas.

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:05.850
There are lots of shops, too.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:09.330
Though most of them only 
sell interior decor.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:12.940
The next event will be starting soon,

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.760
so for now, let's work 
hard to raise our levels.

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:18.260
So we can all have a great Christmas!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.810
I'm in heaven!

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:38.310
No! If I keep this up, 
I'll never want to leave here!

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:40.030
That said...

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:44.360
If I bought all this, 
I'd run out of money fast.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:46.620
I really need to start earning more.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:51.610
I still haven't finished that 
last quest I picked up.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:52.580
Guess I'll do that.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.180
[Sixth of Sword - Blaze]!

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:12.430
Kill before I'm killed!

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:18.490
[Last of Sword - Hazy Moon]!

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.800
[First of Sword - Heat Haze]!

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:46.310
I did it! Finally!

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:51.770
<b>[Bewitched Sword] 
A sword possessing five skills that can be used at the cost of HP depletion, MP depletion,
temporary debuff, long-term debuff, or physical restrictions, respectively. 
[Self-Devouring Bewitched Sword - Yukari] 
[STR+30] [Bewitched Sword] [Self-Repair] 
Self-Repair 
Durability recovers indefinitely while the sword is sheathed.</b>

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:50.830
The Self-Devouring Bewitched 
Sword, Yukari...

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:53.740
Let's try you out right away.

00:11:58.180 --> 00:12:00.790
If I recall, this guy has a lot of health.

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:03.170
I'll take you on!

00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:05.620
Self-Devouring Bewitched Sword, Yukari!

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:09.750
What?!

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:16.380
Using this sword makes me look like this?

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:18.840
I can end that by finishing 
this battle quick!

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:22.380
Purple Phantom Blade

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.840
Purple Phantom Blade 
A technique that draws out the Bewitched Sword's true potential.
Unleashes a barrage of strikes, then pierces the opponent with ten Bewitched Swords at once.
In exchange, the user's physical abilities are drastically reduced.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:47.060
Nice! Excellent!

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:49.670
I got some more money, too... Huh?

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.160
Huh?! Wh-What's going on?!

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:01.290
What?!

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.190
Rawr!

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:08.030
Thank you all for coming here today!

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:12.060
It's time to kick off our sixth event!

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.260
As we've already announced,

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:20.520
rare materials and exclusive Christmas items 
are hidden throughout the event field,

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.650
so try your best to find them!

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:24.640
You'll be teleported to 
a random starting point,

00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:27.490
and the event period will 
be two in-game days.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:31.700
Check out the information distributed 
in-game for more details!

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.100
And now, the countdown begins!

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.100
Let's do our best, everyone!

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:39.670
Ten, nine, eight, seven, six, five,

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:37.030
I guess we'll be going into this separately.

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:39.670
So maybe no one will see me 
looking like a child, at least.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:41.630
Something wrong, Kasumi?

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:45.930
four, three, two, one, zero!

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:43.760
Er, no, nothing.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:50.710
A jungle?

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.310
[Machine God]!

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:00.050
[Hydra]!

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.840
[Predator]!

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:04.500
[Deploy Armaments]!

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.070
[Commence Attack]!

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:19.060
I guess monsters like these aren't 
gonna give any skills or items.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:23.960
Sounds like the big boys are showing up!

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.640
Huh? Payne?

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:34.110
Maple?!

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:38.370
I started out fighting with [Machine God],

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:42.610
but since there were so many of them, 
I figured this might work better.

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:45.320
I get that, but...

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:47.880
Aren't you gonna go back 
to your regular form?

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:50.430
N-Not yet... for... reasons...

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:55.490
Because then I won't be able to 
use it again until tomorrow.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:15:00.230
Well, since we met up, how about 
we work together for a while?

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:02.290
Huh? You and me?

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:04.960
It'd be more efficient to 
work as a pair, right?

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.990
Besides, since you clobbered 
me in the fourth event,

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:10.550
I'd like a chance to study how you fight.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:13.570
Oh, please! I'm nowhere near that good!

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:18.350
I should be doing <i>my</i> best to keep 
up with top players like yourself!

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:21.380
I consider it an honor. We pair up, then?

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:23.060
Yes, by all means!

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.870
What the heck is going on here?!

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.000
This is bad!

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:37.450
If those two pair up, the monsters we 
prepared for this event won't stand a chance!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.620
I never would've seen this coming!

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:43.640
Argh! That Maple caught 
us by surprise again!

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:47.670
If I may, I do believe we need 
countermeasures against Maple after all.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.670
Secretary

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:50.760
If nothing changes, the game's 
balance will be thrown off-kilter.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:59.000
Yes, but we can't change the game's 
rules or specs just to weaken Maple.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:03.980
That would wreck the balance 
of the game even more.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:08.260
I think all we can do is buckle 
up and see how things go.

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:09.930
Y-Yes, yes.

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:12.100
I see. Very well.

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:14.830
We will use this event to gather data.

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:16.450
Uh, right, right.

00:16:19.010 --> 00:16:21.950
Remote work isn't as easy as it seems...

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:24.920
That newbie's kinda scary, huh?

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:35.220
There's nothing for me to even do...

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:37.970
But damn, talk about aggressive.

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:41.140
Yeah, you're right. 
They just keep attacking us.

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:44.390
Actually, the one doing 
all the attacking is...

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:49.130
Maple, stop. I hear something.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:50.330
Huh?

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:51.950
Above us!

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:52.820
Incoming!

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.840
Oh, gosh, there are so many!

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:01.220
Looks like it's finally my turn!

00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:08.290
W-Wow...

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:12.270
I wonder who's faster, him or Sally...

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:17.590
What do you want me to do?

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:19.100
You can stay there!

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:21.680
Just stop any monsters 
coming at me from below!

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.080
Got it!

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.970
Careful, Maple!

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:41.660
What is this sticky stuff?! Is it honey?!

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:42.850
Maple!

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.300
Looks like it causes some 
kind of status effect!

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:49.630
If I get hit with a piercing 
attack now, I might be done for!

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:50.980
You're sharing that openly?

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:53.130
Okay, I'll take care of the rest!

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:56.840
[Holy Rain]!

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:07.710
That's a new skill I just gained.

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:10.300
I won't keep any secrets, either.

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:17.550
Looks like the boss is here!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:26.540
[Sword of Judgment]!

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.000
[Wind Cutter]!

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:35.210
Thanks, Oboro!

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:35.920
Web User I 
Uses webs. After level 5, the webs can be stretched. Firing range is five meters. Webs can be shot from hands and feet. Using a second time deactivates the skill.

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:38.910
Ooh, I got the [Web User] skill!

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:40.170
Sounds fun!

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:42.450
What's that?

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:46.490
Is this one of the event items?

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.990
I guess I'm stuck like this for ten minutes.

00:18:57.300 --> 00:19:00.280
I'd rather avoid using this 
skill in front of anyone.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:02.050
Huh? Kasumi?

00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:04.670
Shin?!

00:19:06.730 --> 00:19:09.470
You never saw this! Understand?!

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:12.900
K-Kasumi! Your wrap! It's gonna fall off!

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:14.090
Huh?

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:22.970
<b>—Two Days Later—</b>

00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:22.970
The event's almost over.

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:26.180
And we never got to see Payne.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:28.780
Where the hell is he, anyway?

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:32.310
Maple!

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.220
Payne!

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:35.320
It's Dread and Drag.

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:38.030
Good to see you again!

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:41.770
This is far enough. 
Thanks for everything, Maple.

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:43.070
I should be thanking you!

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:46.260
And don't forget what we talked about, okay?

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:48.260
Yeah, of course.

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:50.840
Yo, Payne, what's goin' on?

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:53.080
What did she mean by "what we talked about"?

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:56.540
Well, actually...

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:59.010
Merry Christmas!

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:01.720
Merry Christmas!

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:03.320
This is what she meant?

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:04.910
Maple invited us.

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:09.560
It's a party to celebrate the event's ending, 
Christmas, and the New Year.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:13.590
We're supposed to be rivals, though...

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:16.090
Oh, it's fine, Markus.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:19.210
Even Mii seems to be 
friendly with Maple now.

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:20.440
Right, Mii?

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:21.650
Y-Yes.

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:26.990
Okay, everyone! 
Did you bring your gift boxes?

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:30.500
Yeah, and I haven't looked 
inside yet, as you requested.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:32.220
We haven't, either.

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:35.210
It's the 25th now, 
so they should finally open!

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:38.800
I guess everybody who took 
part in the event got one.

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:42.640
If my gift makes me super strong,

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:45.810
I might be able to beat 
you next time, Sally.

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:47.390
That's what I should say to you.

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:50.140
Okay, let's all open them together!

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:52.960
Is everybody ready?

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:55.320
Ready, set... open!

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:59.610
What is all this?

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:02.070
<i>These</i> are our Christmas gifts?

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:05.810
Kasumi, why don't you try using that katana?

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.610
I bet a child's costume would 
look great on you, then.

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:10.910
I told you not to bring that up!

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:13.730
Is this the admins' idea of a joke?

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:17.720
It looks like they do function 
as weapons and armor, though.

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:21.130
You're right. They're pretty 
high-spec, actually.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:25.970
These could be pretty useful... 
if you can overlook the seasonal theme.

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:28.260
Nice! I like this!

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:29.800
But Maple...

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:34.520
How come only I got one 
that looks like this?!

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:37.340
I'm pretty sure the boxes' 
contents are random.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:41.830
So you just happened to 
pick up a rare one, Maple.

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:43.110
Way to go!

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:45.730
You look great in it, Maple!

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:48.220
Oh... You think so?

00:21:49.630 --> 00:21:51.830
It's just the kind of thing 
we'd expect from you.

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:53.210
Typical Maple.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:54.540
Yep.

00:21:55.850 --> 00:21:58.250
Well, now that we know what our gifts are...

00:21:59.030 --> 00:22:01.150
To many more adventures ahead!

